{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.CpViolationSpectralForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.CpViolationSpectralForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.physical_deltaCP_eq_zero_of_real_characters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.physical_deltaCP_eq_zero_of_real_characters","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L123-L132","doc":"The carrier's one consequence, stated so the class is not write-only:\nunder the conjecture, real characters give no physical CP violation.\nComposes the carrier with `deltaCP_eq_zero_of_real_characters`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CPViolationSpectralForm.spectral_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CPViolationSpectralForm.spectral_form","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L121-L121","doc":"The identification the conjecture asserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CPViolationSpectralForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CPViolationSpectralForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CPViolationSpectralForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CPViolationSpectralForm","kind":"class","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L95-L121","doc":"**Conjecture carrier (§3b): the spectral form of `δ_CP`.**\n\nThe conjecture is an IDENTIFICATION — that the CP-violating discriminant of\na hadronic braid *is* the imaginary part of the alternating/symmetric\ncharacter ratio. Stating it needs a `δ_CP` on the left that is not already\n*defined* as that ratio, and this file's `deltaCP` is exactly that\ndefinition. So the physical discriminant enters as a PARAMETER, supplied by\nthe caller; asserting the identity against `deltaCP` itself would be a\nself-assuming projection (§3b-cond item 5).\n\nThe field is content-bearing: it is false for any `physicalDeltaCP`\ndisagreeing with `deltaCP` at a single `W`, so `⟨True⟩`-style inhabitation\nis impossible.\n\n**No instance is provided, and that is the honest open state** (§3b-tax).\nConstructing one requires an independently-defined CP-violating\ndiscriminant, which the corpus does not have —\n`observations/complex-chirality-rotation.lean:44` records the numerical\nbound `δ_CP = O(θ²)` as future work. Per the `.md`, a proof also needs\n`R_ℂ`-enrichment uniqueness and a match of `θ_res` to the Wolfenstein\nparameterisation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:cp-violation-spectral-form","label":"conj:cp-violation-spectral-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.deltaCP_eq_zero_of_real_characters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.deltaCP_eq_zero_of_real_characters","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L80-L93","doc":"**Real characters give no CP violation.**\n\nIf both Wedderburn-block characters are real — the amphicheiral and\nreal-`q` configurations — then the discriminant vanishes identically.\n\nThis is the falsifiable content the `.md` names: an amphicheiral hadron\nexhibiting CP violation would contradict it. Both hypotheses are used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.deltaCP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.deltaCP","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L36-L39","doc":"The CP-violating discriminant as the imaginary part of the\nalternating/symmetric ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.sym_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.sym_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.chiSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.chiSym","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.chiAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.chiAlt","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.WedderburnComplexCharacters","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L29-L34","doc":"Wedderburn-block characters as complex numbers under the\ncomplexified substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.modulus_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.modulus_pos","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.q_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.q_phase","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.q_modulus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.q_modulus","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ComplexSubstrate","kind":"class","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/cp-violation-spectral-form.lean#L22-L27","doc":"Conjectural class: the substrate parameter is complexified, with\nthe alternating-block character carrying the residual phase. ","signatureChunk":0}]}